{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Mrs Rao, please come in. I will check the BP and pulse before doctor sees you.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Arm loose, madam. One forty-eight over ninety-two. Pulse seventy-eight. I have put it on the paper.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Thank you, sister. Ma, shoes there only.",
  "[SEG0005] person_4 (DOCTOR): Morning, Mrs Rao. This is the routine BP review, yes?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (DOCTOR): How is the sleep?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Doctor, before that, the parking fellow was arguing, so we got late, sorry.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (DOCTOR): It is alright. Any headache?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (DOCTOR): Giddiness?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0014] person_4 (DOCTOR): Chest pain?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes, not really.",
  "[SEG0016] person_4 (DOCTOR): Breathlessness when you walk?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_4 (DOCTOR): Feeling tired?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (DOCTOR): Since how long?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Two weeks.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ma, no, you have been saying this from at least two months, after you left the morning walk.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Weeks.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): Alright, we will keep it as roughly two weeks to two months. Not sorting it now.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (DOCTOR): You are on amlodipine five milligram for the pressure. Daily?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Alternate.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (DOCTOR): Every other day?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She says the full dose makes the ankles a little heavy, so she made it alternate herself.",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (DOCTOR): Ankle swelling today?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (DOCTOR): Let me look. No, ankles are not swollen. I will not do a full examination.",
  "[SEG0033] person_4 (DOCTOR): Atorvastatin twenty milligram at night, for cholesterol. Still taking?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Stopped.",
  "[SEG0035] person_4 (DOCTOR): Why?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Online.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Some website said statins spoil the liver. I told her not to stop, she did not listen.",
  "[SEG0038] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any muscle pain?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0040] person_4 (DOCTOR): Acidity or loose motions?",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Also, doctor, Papa's diabetes tablets are in the same steel box. Metformin.",
  "[SEG0043] person_4 (DOCTOR): Mrs Rao, you are swallowing his sugar tablets?",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): They are metformin five hundred, morning and night. Those are his, Ma.",
  "[SEG0046] person_4 (DOCTOR): Do not take his tablets. Only your own box.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0048] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any other medicine?",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0050] person_4 (DOCTOR): Right. I will not scold you. Today's pressure is a bit high, most likely because the amlodipine is on alternate days. From tonight, take five milligram every day.",
  "[SEG0051] person_4 (DOCTOR): We will repeat the lipid profile and the liver function test. Come in one month, then we decide on the statin. Do not start it yourself before that.",
  "[SEG0052] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I will bring her. And I will keep Papa's metformin separate.",
  "[SEG0053] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine."
 ],
